WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.035
-I want to ask about this,
because, you know, obviously,

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you're running against a
Republican right now,

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.171
they would probably be attacking
your lack of experience,

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you're in this situation
where even progressives,

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.342 size:84% position:42%
who like your ideas,
are concerned about it.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you address this
fact that you

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
aren't coming from
a political background,

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.048
especially at a time where
someone's in The White House

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
who didn't have
a lot of experience,

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it looks like
it's not going great?

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:22.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, but what I want to say
is -- Donald Trump is,

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.625
first and foremost,
a real-estate developer, right?

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:29.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who ran to give himself
and people in his tax bracket

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.598 size:88% position:44% line:92%
a huge income-tax break.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm somebody
who grew up the daughter

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:37.537
of a single mother in a
five-flight one-bedroom walkup,

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
somebody who has
spent the last 17 years

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:45.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
and used my celebrity
to fight for LGBTQ equality

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
and for women's rights
and abortion rights

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
and most especially
to fight for better funding

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
and more equal funding
for New York's public schools.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:55.388
And I think that that's the
kind of progressive fighter

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
that New York needs
leading it right now.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:01:01.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
We already have a corrupt
corporate Republican

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:01.828 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in the White House.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
We don't need a
corrupt corporate Democrat

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.366 size:84% position:42% line:92%
opposing him in Albany.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:09.803 size:88% position:44%
-So, I want to get to an
issue that we both agree

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:12.505 size:78% position:39%
and I think everybody
in the city agrees --

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
the subways
are -- they're not good.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:18.011 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's one, I think,
you've addressed.

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.248
And, obviously, you know,
the subway is a lifeblood

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a lot of people
that have to get to work.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:24.651 size:78% position:39% line:92%
This a serious issue.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.187
-The subway is literally
what New York City runs on.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.221 line:92%
-It's literally what it runs on.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:33.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
And how do you even go about
trying to address

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
this issue that
not just through --

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be fair, has been
deteriorating for years,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just due to
the Cuomo administration.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, but look at
what's happened

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.135 size:88% position:44% line:92%
in the last seven years.

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:45.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
Delays have tripled
under Andrew Cuomo.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:46.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've got the
worst on-time record now

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:49.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
of any major transit system
in the entire country.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:53.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We did have that pizza rat.
That was a nice moment.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.914 line:92%
That happened on his watch.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was the first governor
to have a pizza rat.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But he has watched
the steady decline.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's siphoned off hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:06.426
for pet projects that have
absolutely nothing to do

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.627 size:75% position:38% line:92%
with transportation.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.495 line:92%
And the fact of the matter is --

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:10.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
like so many of
the issues that we face,

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:14.200
the problems that we face in
New York, we know the solution.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, right now, we have
a governor who doesn't have

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:18.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
the political will
to make it happen.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.574
-The solution being we need more
money put into the subways.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:25.378
-The solution being we have
a really comprehensive plan

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.715
for how to fix them, to replace
the 1930s-era signals,

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:32.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
to replace the trains
from the '60s and the '70s,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
to run cars closer together
so that we can get more trains

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.825
on the system so we're all
not jammed in like sardines.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:43.930
But Andrew Cuomo doesn't want to
enact a tax on millionaires,

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they're some of
his biggest donors

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he doesn't want
to alienate them.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
And his they're not
people who ride the subway.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
He himself is not someone
who rides the subway.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:55.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's been on the subway twice
since taking office.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.911 size:75% position:38%
As somebody who's on
the subway every day

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:00.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
and knows firsthand
how terrible it is

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:03.583
and how it's getting
worse and worse month by month,

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is not something we have
a choice about fixing,

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:06.786 line:92%
the New York City subway,

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:10.123
and this is not something
that we can delay fixing.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.558 line:92%
It's only going to get harder

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:14.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
and more expensive
to fix the longer we wait.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.663 size:78% position:39%
-Is it -- has it been
disappointing for you

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:18.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is it what you expected
that a lot of

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:22.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
establishment Democrats
are throwing their support

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.571 size:81% position:41% line:92%
behind Governor Cuomo?

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.438 line:92%
You know, people like Joe Biden

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:28.441
and people like Hillary Clinton
are supporting him.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that what you expected
or a disappointment?

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is exactly
what we expected.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:35.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a total
insurgent campaign.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:37.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a
people-powered campaign.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.219 line:92%
And this is a campaign that

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:41.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're talking
to people about issues.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're talking
to people about things

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:46.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they care about,
like legalizing marijuana.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:49.562 size:84% position:42%
I know your audience
doesn't care about that

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:50.630 size:75% position:38% line:92%
issue in particular.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.364 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:55.301
But we have to legalize
marijuana for a lot of reasons,

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also because
it's a racial-justice issue,

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
because people across
all ethnicities and races

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
use marijuana
at roughly the same rates,

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:07.080
but 80% of the arrests
are of black and Latino people.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's just
the tip of the iceberg

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.984 size:78% position:39%
of the justice reform
that we need to do.

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:14.554
We need to stop the overpolicing
of communities of color.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have to
stop mass incarceration.

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:19.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when we're talking about
mass incarceration,

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're talking about
mass incarceration

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:22.295 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of people of color.

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:25.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the subway
is also mass incarceration,

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:26.799 line:92%
if you've been on it recently.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-At the moment.
At the moment, it is.

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:31.471 size:84% position:42%
-At the moment, it is.
It's all very exciting.

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's very exciting to
you have here,

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
both because of
the political message

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:37.443
that you're pushing forward --
Also, we were talking backstage.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:38.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do want to
mention this briefly.

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:40.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had never seen
"Sex and the City."

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
My wife made me
start watching it this year.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're on Season 4.
-I'm so sorry. Yes.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very much enjoying it.
-Good, good, good.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.021 line:92%
-But I'm really bothered,

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:51.291
because I feel like I have a
really good impression of Steve.

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:55.461
But I feel like it's a problem,
because I feel like the window

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.530
is closed, as far as that
being an effective tool.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:02.535
Like, no one is dying to hear
a Steve impression right now.

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:03.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I feel like
since you're here,

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a unique
opportunity to do it.

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would be so thrilled.
-Okay, great. Are you ready?

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:11.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wish we -- Do we have
a Brooklyn Bridge, you know,

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:11.844 size:75% position:38% line:92%
photo that we can --

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is close enough, I feel.
-It's close enough.

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah yeah.
-All right. Go ahead.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:15.214 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
All right. Okay.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ As Steve ] What's going on
with us, Miranda?

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:22.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I can't figure out
what we're doing.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:22.922 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Should we get a dog?

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's very good.
-Thank you.

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
That means a lot.
You made me feel very good.

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:30.463
You just made me feel very good.
-That was beautiful.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:34.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give it up for
Cynthia Nixon, everybody.

